/-
AtFullSide/K1/OpeningEntries.lean: THE 544 ENTRIES OF THE WRITTEN BOOK ON THE COINS OF THE OPENING's
SENDER (the owner ⟨⟨1, some 0, 1, .K1⟩, 0⟩), AS WRITTEN LISTS, each held by an evaluation in Lean's
kernel against its piece of rawAheadW (AtFullSide/K14/RawAheadWritten.lean): 335 that spend, 209 that
carry. Public data alone: names, addresses, numbers. Eight definitions; the rest are theorems.

  opener           the owner
  shortB, shortD   rawAheadW's written pieces in front of and behind the chain of segments' entries
  openSA, openSB   the spending entries: of the stretches' (334); of the written pieces in front (1)
  openCC, openCD   the carried entries: of the chain of segments' (207); of the pieces behind (2)
  openS, openC     the two lists
  filter_whole     a filter of rawAheadW, piece by piece
  eight evaluations (…_spend, …_carry)   each piece's filter is its written list, or empty
  spends_open, carries_open   rawAheadW's spending | carried entries with that owner ARE the two lists
  open_bent        the comparison can fail: one count bent

How made. The lists were printed by a program from rawAheadW's own value and are compared here with
it by the kernel, names and all: a fault in the print fails the build.

Limits. The limits of RawAheadWritten.lean. The full size alone. Options are raised in front of the
evaluations. In the side library, because it imports files of it. No property of the protocol is
claimed.
-/
